{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/903933-vampire-2e-the-kiss","id":903933,"title":"Vampire 2E The Kiss","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-30T21:02:57-07:00","id":903933,"title":"Vampire 2E The Kiss","content":"Hey everyone,<br /> <br /> I was debating with another player regarding 2E Vampire and Hunters. According to the Kiss it as quoted from the text effects the following things as pleasurable and granting the Swooning Condition: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mortal bitten subtly gains the Swooning Condition (see p. 306). The bonuses and penalties for Swooning apply to the vampire\u2019s Discipline rolls. With a subtle bite, the vampire can take one Vitae per turn, and may lick the wound afterwards, leaving no trace of her feeding. At Storyteller discretion, particularly dramatic feedings can cause Persistent Conditions. For this reason, many vampire hunters have the Scarred or Swooning Conditions. On the other hand, so do many devoted blood dolls. In reference to the effects of a bite, the word \u201cmortal\u201d applies to humans, ghouls, warlocks, and other things that are mostly human. </div> </div> </div>So, from my reading of this, the following are affected: Hunters, Mages, Ghouls, Wolf-blooded, Sleepwalkers, normal folk.<br /> <br /> Am I understanding this correctly?<br /> <br /> The latest hunter update seems to state they are immune, but they are also not 2E so, I am not sure how much that is worth.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Teamwork makes the dream work!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4720-taldorblackfire","name":"Taldorblackfire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:35:41-07:00","id":903966,"title":"","content":"Yes, that's pretty much accurate. I don't know why Hunters would be immune, specifically, unless they're from a Conspiracy that makes them truly inhuman.<br /> <br /> Also note that other supernatural creatures aren't immune so much as the vampire has to make extra effort to inflict the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T03:45:06-07:00","id":904070,"title":"","content":"I also believe that the Mortal Remains update came out after GMC, but before Vampire 2e/Strix Chronicles came out. So there's a lot of assumptions based on 1e. The 1e Kiss, while it made you feel good no matter what you were, its main function was to blur your memory of feeding. If you were immune to the Kiss, it just means you remember each moment of being fed on. Which is thematically appropriate for Hunters. You kinda need to know you're dealing with a monster, after all, if you're going to hunt them. <br /> <br /> In 2e Vampire, the Kiss simply works differently, so you can't assume Mortal Remains holds true. In fact, I don't see any mind-blurring effects going on here. So, there's no reason for them to be immune to the 2e Kiss, since it has no effect on the ability to remember vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T09:20:04-07:00","id":904214,"title":"","content":"As far as I am aware, Nothing is immune to the pleasure of the Kiss. Anything inherently human, Hunters, ghouls, The things you listed all gain the swooning condition after being fed on subtly. It isnt memory wiping, but often the person doesn't know that there were fangs and blood loss involved, just the pleasure. <br /> <br /> You can spend a willpower to inflict swooning on non-human things. Vampires, werewolves, changlings. Ect. <br /> (Same goes for the violent feeding and scared condition )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}